/-!
# Polars of the twisted secant quintic `kleinTwS`

Explicit polar coefficients `kleinTwSP j` (the coefficient of `t^j` in `kleinTwS (c + t • u)`)
and the coefficients `kleinTwSD i` / `kleinTwSDD_ij` of the `u`-monomials `u_i^2` / `u_i u_j` in
the second polar `kleinTwSP 2`.  With `Work.MotK.KleinTwPolar` these give the twisted analogue of
the split identity **I5** of `Submission/Work/MotK/CensusFibre/SecPolar.lean`, which is the input of
the T-twisted ruling identity `Work.MotK.KleinTwRuleMem`.

The twisted secant `kleinTwS` is the Kummer twist (`KleinTwData`) of the split secant quintic `s`
under `x_l = w^l y_l` (`w^5 = h`).  The `ℤ/5`-grading `deg y_l = l` forces the second partials of
the twisted secant to lie in the ideal of the twisted quadrics; the resulting certificates are
proved in `Work.MotK.KleinTwPolar`, where the `h`-powers are justified as well.

Generated by `_ktrwork/gen_defs.py` (sympy, exact arithmetic over `ℤ[a,b,h]`).
-/

